1
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,205
Ms. Zheng.

2
00:01:57,205 --> 00:01:59,680
Did your boss say when he'll be finished?

3
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,280
I've been waiting for almost an hour.

4
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,120
I'm sorry.
Mr. Fu is busy at the training center.

5
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:06,160
It may take him a while to get here too.

6
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:09,322
Have some water while you wait.

7
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,553
More water?

8
00:02:23,898 --> 00:02:26,208
- Fu Ming Yu is such a jerk!
- Fu Ming Yu is such a jerk!

9
00:02:26,986 --> 00:02:28,355
A double act?

10
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,945
Who's copying me?

11
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:36,560
[Episode 9]
[Then We're Even]

12
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:39,840
[Briefing Room for SDA No.1 Simulator]

13
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,408
Fifty.

14
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:23,099
Thirty. Twenty. Retard.

15
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:35,966
Thank you for your hard work.

16
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,457
What are the results?

17
00:03:50,457 --> 00:03:55,640
There's indeed a seven-minute overlap
with Captain Fan's situation that day.

18
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:58,560
I believe Captain Fan did her absolute best.

19
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,480
Alright, I'm aware of the situation.

20
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:05,199
Still, do compare the flight data again
when you're back.

21
00:04:05,199 --> 00:04:07,864
- No problem. I'll head out then.
- Sure, take care.

22
00:04:07,864 --> 00:04:09,523
- Okay.
- Goodbye, Mr. Fu.

23
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:22,320
[Let's have dinner together tomorrow.]

24
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:24,348
- What is it?
- Let me brief you.

25
00:04:24,348 --> 00:04:27,926
I've notified the relevant leaders
and the Safety Committee.

26
00:04:27,926 --> 00:04:31,551
Also, Mrs. He has set up
a last-minute dinner for you tonight.

27
00:04:31,551 --> 00:04:33,015
Since it's quite a long drive,

28
00:04:33,015 --> 00:04:36,040
and some of our key board members
will be there,

29
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,680
you'll need to get there early to prepare.

30
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,945
Let's head out now.

31
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,768
- Also, tell Zheng You An not to wait.
- Okay.

32
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,877
<i>I don't have time.</i>

33
00:04:47,363 --> 00:04:48,923
- Let's go.
- Okay.

34
00:04:52,024 --> 00:04:53,379
Instructor Fang.

35
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:59,230
You're certainly diligent.
I haven't even sipped my coffee yet.

36
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,113
I should let you know.

37
00:05:02,113 --> 00:05:05,176
You have simulator sessions
for the next two days, right?

38
00:05:05,176 --> 00:05:07,680
- Yes.
- But the company has other plans.

39
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,680
All training must be suspended.

40
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,000
- Why?
- Mr. Fu's orders.

41
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:16,047
Him again.

42
00:05:17,691 --> 00:05:20,867
Come on, let's start. I'll skip the coffee.

43
00:05:40,397 --> 00:05:42,394
Excuse me.

44
00:05:42,394 --> 00:05:45,044
It's been almost three hours.
When will he be back?

45
00:05:45,044 --> 00:05:47,083
Sorry, I was just about to tell you.

46
00:05:47,083 --> 00:05:49,924
Mr. Fu has other arrangements today.
He won't be returning.

47
00:05:49,924 --> 00:05:52,694
- He's not coming back?
- No, he's not.

48
00:05:54,154 --> 00:05:55,618
Thank you.

49
00:05:57,331 --> 00:05:59,906
What kind of person is he?

50
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,640
- Hope to see you at our school again.
- Thank you.

51
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,664
- One at a time.
- Good work, everyone.

52
00:06:06,664 --> 00:06:09,160
We can find a place to grab a bite later.

53
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,345
If you have any questions, feel free to ask me.

54
00:06:11,345 --> 00:06:12,400
- Is that okay?
- Great!

55
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,625
- Where should we eat?
- Will it be too much trouble?

56
00:06:13,625 --> 00:06:15,609
Somewhere nearby. Let's find a good place.

57
00:06:15,609 --> 00:06:17,673
- Sure.
- I know a hot pot place nearby.

58
00:06:17,673 --> 00:06:19,000
- Sounds good.
- Let's go then.

59
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,720
- Okay.
- Captain Yue.

60
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,080
Excuse me.

61
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:26,226
Mr. Xie, thank you so much.
The students were so welcoming.

62
00:06:26,226 --> 00:06:28,421
It's all thanks to the school's support.
I'm truly grateful.

63
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:29,960
Thank you for your hard work, Captain Yue.

64
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:34,260
- Actually, I wanted to ask you about someone.
- Go ahead.

65
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:38,880
It's about the person
you just mentioned, Ruan Si Xian.

66
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:43,816
- You...
- We were classmates.

67
00:06:45,667 --> 00:06:46,849
Okay.

68
00:06:52,010 --> 00:06:54,422
- Fu Ming Yu is such a jerk!
- Fu Ming Yu is such a jerk!

69
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,360
A double act?

70
00:06:57,296 --> 00:06:58,336
Who's copying me?

71
00:06:58,336 --> 00:07:02,480
I've put up with him for far too long.
He even stood me up today.

72
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,680
Come out tonight.
I'll tell you about it over drinks.

73
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,280
Why are you going to Manchester?

74
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,120
I'll let you go then.

75
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,840
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

76
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:34,452
It's just that
you were cursing pretty loudly just now.

77
00:07:35,279 --> 00:07:37,680
So what if you heard it?

78
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:40,269
It's not like you're going to tell on me.

79
00:07:40,269 --> 00:07:44,597
I just wondered who had the nerve to say that

80
00:07:44,597 --> 00:07:46,640
on Fu Ming Yu's turf.

81
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:48,720
Quite spot on!

82
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:53,548
Exactly. I knew you hated Fu Ming Yu too.

83
00:07:53,548 --> 00:07:55,692
Come on. Let's go for a drink tonight.

84
00:07:55,692 --> 00:07:58,396
It's rare to find someone else
who hates Fu Ming Yu.

85
00:07:58,396 --> 00:08:01,080
I'll pass. I'm meeting friends tonight.

86
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,545
A boyfriend?

87
00:08:02,545 --> 00:08:03,640
No.

88
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,240
Then let's all get to know each other.

89
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,360
Drinking is more fun with a crowd.
It's my treat.

90
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,800
I really can't.
Besides, I can't drink while on duty.

91
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,760
Right, you're a pilot.

92
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,120
Then you can just have water.

93
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,160
Let's go. I'm a very easygoing person.

94
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:20,063
- No, I really--
- Let's grab drinks tonight and just chill.

95
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:24,200
- Sorry for being late.
- Captain Yue.

96
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,640
- Captain Yue.
- Sorry, everyone.

97
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:28,126
I had to change out of my uniform,
so I got held up for a bit.

98
00:08:28,126 --> 00:08:30,160
I'm really sorry.

99
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,680
- Please, take the head seat.
- No.

100
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,634
Please. Sit down.

101
00:08:33,634 --> 00:08:35,138
Listen, everyone.

102
00:08:35,138 --> 00:08:37,843
Now that we're having dinner,
let's treat each other like friends.

103
00:08:37,843 --> 00:08:40,426
Really, not like earlier in that lecture hall.

104
00:08:40,426 --> 00:08:43,743
Or say, we become colleagues
after your graduation.

105
00:08:43,743 --> 00:08:46,968
At most, I'll be mentoring rookies.

106
00:08:46,968 --> 00:08:48,511
You might call me mentor, but that's it.

107
00:08:48,511 --> 00:08:50,256
Then we'll call you mentor.

108
00:08:50,256 --> 00:08:53,520
- Mentor!
- No, you don't have to.

109
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,424
I gathered everyone here today

110
00:08:55,424 --> 00:08:59,960
because I know you all have questions,
but we ran out of time earlier.

111
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,200
- Right.
- Right.

112
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:05,000
Now that we're all together,
let's chat over some drinks.

113
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,092
- Sure.
- Sounds good.

114
00:09:06,092 --> 00:09:08,400
So, have you ordered any drinks yet?

115
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,759
- No.
- Not yet.

116
00:09:09,759 --> 00:09:12,680
Okay, I figured. I'll go get some.
You guys sit here for a bit.

117
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,209
- Okay.
- Okay.

118
00:09:18,795 --> 00:09:21,459
- What are you doing here?
- To steal your recruits.

119
00:09:21,459 --> 00:09:23,682
If I waited until after the presentation,

120
00:09:23,682 --> 00:09:27,066
you would've snapped up all the best recruits.

121
00:09:29,963 --> 00:09:33,240
See? You're all natural for flight attendants.

122
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:36,952
Hello, everyone. I'm Jiang Zi Yue,
a purser at Hengshi Air.

123
00:09:36,952 --> 00:09:38,625
You can call me Zi Yue.

124
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:41,216
- Hello, Zi Yue.
- Hello, Zi Yue!

125
00:09:42,195 --> 00:09:45,865
Why don't you chat with the students?
I'll go order the drinks.

126
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:53,924
He's the one who asked me back
to shoot for him.

127
00:09:53,924 --> 00:09:57,148
And yet, every single time...

128
00:09:57,148 --> 00:10:01,280
Every single time! He's never satisfied.

129
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,880
Fine.

130
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:05,200
If he doesn't like it, I'll redo it.

131
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:10,063
For this latest proposal,
I pulled several all-nighters.

132
00:10:10,063 --> 00:10:12,804
I waited for him all afternoon.

133
00:10:12,804 --> 00:10:14,480
And the result?

134
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:17,023
He didn't even glance at it.

135
00:10:17,023 --> 00:10:18,360
I--

136
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,318
Please enjoy.

137
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,080
I just don't understand.

138
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:29,463
How can someone get more obnoxious
as they grow up?

139
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:32,318
More obnoxious as they grow up.

140
00:10:33,114 --> 00:10:35,784
You have to deal with him every day.
You poor thing.

141
00:10:36,948 --> 00:10:39,812
I'm going to the restroom.
Take it easy with the drinks.

142
00:10:39,812 --> 00:10:41,272
Don't drink too fast.

143
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,773
I'll be right back.

144
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:48,313
Why are you hanging out with her?

145
00:10:48,313 --> 00:10:51,173
I don't know. I'm so annoyed.

146
00:10:51,955 --> 00:10:54,859
On my way to the company today, I ran into her.

147
00:10:54,859 --> 00:10:58,186
She insisted on dragging me here to drink.
I turned her down a dozen times.

148
00:10:58,186 --> 00:11:00,330
In the end, she got her way.

149
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:02,955
Does she know who you are?

150
00:11:02,955 --> 00:11:04,414
Of course not.

151
00:11:05,619 --> 00:11:06,883
That's good then.

152
00:11:06,883 --> 00:11:09,907
Does your mom still send you money every month?

153
00:11:09,907 --> 00:11:11,972
Once every two or three months.

154
00:11:11,972 --> 00:11:15,064
But I haven't used that card.
I never even checked it.

155
00:11:16,377 --> 00:11:19,800
Then what's your stance now?

156
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:22,665
Are you going to mend the relationship or...?

157
00:11:22,665 --> 00:11:24,490
Let's not talk about this now.

158
00:11:24,490 --> 00:11:26,793
Right now, I need to get her out of here.

159
00:11:26,793 --> 00:11:28,494
Go on. Keep an eye on her.

160
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:47,182
Wake up, Zheng You An.

161
00:11:53,057 --> 00:11:54,696
You're so drunk.

162
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,737
[Fu Ming Yu]

163
00:12:00,737 --> 00:12:02,308
Come here.

164
00:12:08,558 --> 00:12:10,230
<i>Come here.</i>

165
00:12:12,875 --> 00:12:14,527
Go to Fly Pub.

166
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,520
- It hurts.
- What are you doing?

167
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,377
Helping you take care of your friend.

168
00:12:29,377 --> 00:12:31,480
No need. We're leaving.

169
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:34,264
Come on. It's still early.

170
00:12:34,264 --> 00:12:36,040
Why is your friend so drunk?

171
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,680
I'll tell you why.

172
00:12:38,363 --> 00:12:43,080
Today, she broke a man's leg.
She's going to jail.

173
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:45,176
She's here to drown her sorrows.

174
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:49,785
- You're quite the joker, gorgeous.
- I'm not joking.

175
00:12:49,785 --> 00:12:52,428
I know a lot more about
beating someone up than she does.

176
00:12:52,428 --> 00:12:54,732
Want to put it to the test?

177
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:58,270
No, thanks. I'll be going now. Bye.

178
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:09,129
- I don't get it. Why are you so mad--
- Can you keep your voice down?

179
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,520
I only came here for tomorrow's presentation.

180
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:15,240
Jiang Zi Yue, we should stop beating
around the bush. You should be more honest.

181
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:18,720
After we got back from Australia,
you told me we were officially dating.

182
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,880
I understand keeping it private,
but why act like you're single?

183
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,921
That's my call.

184
00:13:23,921 --> 00:13:26,881
Well, guess a lot of things are my call too.

185
00:13:26,881 --> 00:13:30,297
Does that mean I can say whatever I want?

186
00:13:31,107 --> 00:13:32,635
Captain Yue.

187
00:13:40,196 --> 00:13:41,832
Yes, you're right.

188
00:13:42,594 --> 00:13:43,840
I was wrong.

189
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,435
What were you wrong about?

190
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:50,479
I should have considered your feelings, right?

191
00:13:51,515 --> 00:13:55,361
But you saw it yourself. Just now,
including me, there were twelve of us.

192
00:13:55,361 --> 00:13:58,789
Eight men and four women.
What could I have possibly done?

193
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:04,960
Come here. Just think of me as
a child. I'm being rebellious.

194
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:08,148
- Then why were you so mean to me?
- I...

195
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:10,720
I'm sorry.

196
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,675
Let's go.

197
00:14:24,091 --> 00:14:26,076
Mr. Fu, you're here. They're inside.

198
00:14:26,076 --> 00:14:28,429
- Okay, thank you.
- No problem.

199
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,917
You wanted to drink?

200
00:14:37,595 --> 00:14:40,531
No. She felt like drinking.

201
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:51,087
So she's the reason that you called me here.

202
00:14:51,087 --> 00:14:55,120
Why else? She's drinking because of you.

203
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,880
Hurry up and take her away.
I'm exhausted. I'm going home to sleep.

204
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,585
Why do you say it's because of me?

205
00:14:59,585 --> 00:15:01,520
That's what she said.

206
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,505
You made her cry, so deal with it yourself.

207
00:15:03,505 --> 00:15:06,978
I've made many women cry.
Do I have to apologize to every one?

208
00:15:15,427 --> 00:15:17,157
That's not what I meant.

209
00:15:18,818 --> 00:15:22,040
Don't touch me. I have my own driver.

210
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:24,387
I'm cutting all ties with you.

211
00:15:24,387 --> 00:15:28,760
From now on, you take the high road,
and I'll take the narrow one.

212
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:30,680
Wait, no.

213
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:34,120
I'll take the high road,
and you take the narrow one.

214
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:37,745
You don't actually think
everyone in the world likes you, do you?

215
00:15:37,745 --> 00:15:39,610
You're really full of yourself.

216
00:15:39,610 --> 00:15:43,120
In this world, plenty of people don't like you.
So many people don't like you!

217
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,960
Get her home safely
and let me know when she does.

218
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,130
Yes, sir.

219
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,280
Don't let her get out of the car halfway.

220
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,920
- Understood, Mr. Fu.
- Go on.

221
00:16:02,005 --> 00:16:03,614
Hey, gorgeous.

222
00:16:04,339 --> 00:16:07,464
- Is your friend gone?
- Go away. Not in the mood.

223
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:10,640
All the more reason to drink if you're upset.

224
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:14,913
I can't stand to see a beauty
looking so sad. Come on.

225
00:16:14,913 --> 00:16:18,537
Good company makes a thousand drinks feel few.

226
00:16:18,537 --> 00:16:20,321
Let's drink until we're wasted!

227
00:16:20,321 --> 00:16:23,280
I'm warning you.
If you keep touching me, I'll slap you.

228
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:25,680
Sir, are you drunk?

229
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:28,145
Want me to take you
to the police station to cool off?

230
00:16:28,145 --> 00:16:29,368
It's right ahead.

231
00:16:29,368 --> 00:16:32,160
No, please. Alright.

232
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,625
Today, for the pretty boss's sake...

233
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:37,449
Next time, gorgeous,
you must give me your WeChat.

234
00:16:37,449 --> 00:16:40,573
Next time? Forget WeChat. Get lost!

235
00:16:41,281 --> 00:16:43,435
What a jerk.

236
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:47,304
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. What could happen?

237
00:16:47,304 --> 00:16:49,280
- Is Fu Ming Yu gone?
- Yes.

238
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,703
I told him to take Zheng You An home.

239
00:16:51,703 --> 00:16:54,911
You let him take another woman home?
You're so open-minded.

240
00:16:54,911 --> 00:16:57,320
Otherwise? It's none of my business.

241
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:01,480
You let him take another woman home,
and say it's none of your business?

242
00:17:24,375 --> 00:17:25,489
Oh my.

243
00:17:26,393 --> 00:17:28,528
I'll get some ice for his face.

244
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:32,419
Tong Le! Get the ice, quick!

245
00:17:42,892 --> 00:17:44,755
Are you all cooled off?

246
00:17:49,221 --> 00:17:51,989
- Yeah.
- Good.

247
00:17:51,989 --> 00:17:53,708
It's time to go home.

248
00:17:55,266 --> 00:17:56,966
I'll take you.

249
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:15,709
<i>Was my slap that powerful?</i>

250
00:18:25,587 --> 00:18:27,594
Is it that funny?

251
00:18:47,461 --> 00:18:49,404
Why are you looking at your hand?

252
00:18:52,898 --> 00:18:54,528
My hand...

253
00:18:55,649 --> 00:18:57,006
It hurts.

254
00:19:02,508 --> 00:19:06,711
"Captain" Ruan, it seems you don't know
that every action has a reaction.

255
00:19:17,097 --> 00:19:18,613
Get in the car.

256
00:19:56,012 --> 00:19:57,697
Goodbye, Mr. Fu.

257
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:15,267
Are you serious? Ruan slapped him?

258
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:21,968
Very well. That was a good slap.
So Ruan has vented.

259
00:20:21,968 --> 00:20:24,152
But won't Fu Ming Yu get angry?

260
00:20:24,152 --> 00:20:26,537
If you were slapped for no reason,
wouldn't you be angry?

261
00:20:26,537 --> 00:20:29,716
What's more, it's the high and mighty Mr. Fu.

262
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:33,611
What should we do?

263
00:20:33,611 --> 00:20:37,753
Now that he's angry, he might settle old scores
and make us pay for the car repairs.

264
00:20:37,753 --> 00:20:40,257
Wait. Don't say "us."

265
00:20:40,257 --> 00:20:42,960
I didn't crash the car. Nor did I hit him.

266
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:47,360
Xuan. You can't just leave me to die.

267
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:51,658
Stop bothering me. I'm doing the accounts.

268
00:20:54,914 --> 00:20:56,508
Wait, that's not right.

269
00:20:56,508 --> 00:20:58,640
Ruan was the one who slapped him.

270
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,640
Love matches start with a quarrel.

271
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:04,664
Maybe that slap
will actually bring them together.

272
00:21:04,664 --> 00:21:06,596
Unless...

273
00:21:06,596 --> 00:21:12,463
this Fu Ming Yu has Stockholm syndrome.

274
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,916
Are you here to see the injured man?

275
00:21:47,572 --> 00:21:51,023
Here, take this.
You'll feel much better tomorrow.

276
00:21:51,023 --> 00:21:52,137
What's this?

277
00:21:52,137 --> 00:21:55,023
Repair serum. It's very effective.

278
00:21:55,023 --> 00:21:56,160
I don't need that.

279
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:03,120
It really works. I use it all the time.

280
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:04,463
Do you get hit that often?

281
00:22:04,463 --> 00:22:05,960
No.

282
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:08,345
Some flight routes have intense UV rays
at high altitude.

283
00:22:08,345 --> 00:22:10,496
My face gets irritated, so I use it a lot.

284
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:11,620
Here.

285
00:22:19,145 --> 00:22:21,268
Then apply it for me.

286
00:22:46,586 --> 00:22:47,836
Does it hurt?

287
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:51,040
What? Are you worried about me?

288
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:53,000
Who said I was?

289
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:57,710
It's not like I'm made of steel.

290
00:22:58,859 --> 00:23:01,060
How on earth did I hit you so hard?

291
00:23:19,811 --> 00:23:21,544
Is it hot in here?

292
00:23:23,473 --> 00:23:25,029
Why is your face so red?

293
00:23:27,378 --> 00:23:30,678
Are you applying medicine or caressing me?

294
00:23:32,195 --> 00:23:33,874
What do you think?

295
00:23:34,610 --> 00:23:36,200
Are you even a woman?

296
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:42,135
If I were a man, one slap from me
would have knocked your brains out.

297
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:48,471
If you were a man,
would I be so indulgent with you?

298
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,560
Um...

299
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:02,497
I'm sorry.

300
00:24:03,113 --> 00:24:08,800
I mistook you for a creep today,
so I hit you a bit too hard.

301
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:13,064
My apologies. Let's just say we're even now.

302
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,494
We can't be even.

303
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:25,380
Fu Ming Yu doesn't seem like the kind of man
who holds a grudge.

304
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:30,753
I'm just praying that he'll be the bigger man.

305
00:24:30,753 --> 00:24:33,120
Hope he won't make me pay for the car repairs.

306
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:37,680
If Ruan loses her job,
I'm willing to give her 2,000 yuan a month

307
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:41,252
for her living expenses
until she finds another job.

308
00:24:41,252 --> 00:24:45,000
2,000 yuan? You're so generous.

309
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,691
I never would have guessed.

310
00:24:46,691 --> 00:24:50,080
But is your salary even enough
to cover your car loan?

311
00:24:51,098 --> 00:24:52,921
Then what should I do?

312
00:24:52,921 --> 00:24:57,745
Have you ever seen an employee
hit their boss and get away with it?

313
00:24:57,745 --> 00:25:01,360
Don't be more worried than she is.
Ruan hasn't even said anything.

314
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:03,585
Yeah, she hasn't.

315
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:06,809
But didn't you say
she looked totally dejected when she left?

316
00:25:06,809 --> 00:25:10,792
She did, but then she started laughing.

317
00:25:10,792 --> 00:25:12,688
She even laughed out loud.

318
00:25:13,419 --> 00:25:15,080
She laughed?

319
00:25:16,715 --> 00:25:20,938
Three years ago, I misunderstood you.

320
00:25:20,938 --> 00:25:23,126
And I said a lot of nasty things.

321
00:25:23,810 --> 00:25:25,753
<i>I don't want to be a flight attendant.</i>

322
00:25:25,753 --> 00:25:27,400
<i>- I want to be--
- The boss's wife?</i>

323
00:25:28,280 --> 00:25:30,040
<i>Keep dreaming.</i>

324
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:32,784
<i>I've seen plenty of these cheap tricks before.</i>

325
00:25:32,784 --> 00:25:36,888
<i>If you have this much time and energy,
focus it on your actual job.</i>

326
00:25:36,888 --> 00:25:39,982
<i>I think you just want a shortcut.</i>

327
00:25:44,485 --> 00:25:47,989
But I didn't know back then
that you were doing it for the Soar Initiative.

328
00:25:47,989 --> 00:25:50,861
All of this was because of my arrogance.

329
00:25:52,139 --> 00:25:55,189
And I didn't show you enough respect.

330
00:25:55,189 --> 00:25:58,795
But I'm glad that through your own effort,

331
00:25:58,795 --> 00:26:01,440
you've become an excellent pilot.

332
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:04,440
If my actions had ruined someone's dream,

333
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:11,840
I'd have to live with that
and feel deeply ashamed of what I did.

334
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:16,338
But even if I had read your letter back then...

335
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:23,480
I'm sorry, the Soar Initiative
would still have been canceled.

336
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:29,316
Because Hengshi Air was facing overstaffing
and aircraft model reforms.

337
00:26:29,316 --> 00:26:35,083
Continuing the Soar Initiative
would have only accelerated layoffs.

338
00:26:36,582 --> 00:26:39,440
It wouldn't have just meant
a few shattered dreams.

339
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:45,387
Countless families would've had to suffer
the fallout along with Hengshi Air.

340
00:26:48,986 --> 00:26:52,450
What do you mean by this now?

341
00:26:52,450 --> 00:26:55,754
Is this some kind of apology convention?

342
00:26:56,496 --> 00:26:58,380
You just said we're even.

343
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,753
I still think I owe you a formal apology.

344
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:09,683
I can't let this one slap
erase the debt I owe you.

345
00:27:11,028 --> 00:27:15,651
I also hope that you can forgive

346
00:27:15,651 --> 00:27:19,741
that arrogant and rude man I was
three years ago.

347
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:31,056
I've long since moved on.

348
00:27:33,011 --> 00:27:34,613
Then we're even.

349
00:27:54,578 --> 00:27:56,948
<i>Is he waiting for me?</i>

350
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:19,436
Ruan, what a coincidence.

351
00:28:20,042 --> 00:28:21,714
Coincidence indeed.

352
00:28:31,187 --> 00:28:33,021
Did you get a cab?

353
00:28:33,841 --> 00:28:35,210
Not yet.

354
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:38,680
Come. Otherwise, you'll be late again.

355
00:28:49,302 --> 00:28:50,866
Thank you.

356
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:04,675
Ruan, are you really pursuing Mr. Fu?

357
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:08,720
Sir, please pull over.

358
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:10,584
Someone wants to get off.

359
00:29:10,584 --> 00:29:13,328
But we're in the middle of nowhere.

360
00:29:13,328 --> 00:29:15,560
- How could you?
- This is just how I am.

361
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,480
Either that, or you shut up.

362
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:49,187
How did I get back?

363
00:29:59,928 --> 00:30:01,601
Who should I ask?

364
00:30:02,599 --> 00:30:04,400
Fu Ming Yu?

365
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,920
How should I explain it to him?

366
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:08,857
Ruan Si Xian?

367
00:30:10,075 --> 00:30:13,819
I just finished badmouthing him to her,
and then he showed up at the pub.

368
00:30:13,819 --> 00:30:15,250
Backstabber.

369
00:30:17,204 --> 00:30:18,744
It has to be you, then.

370
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:22,784
<i>Xuan, I drank a bit too much yesterday.</i>

371
00:30:22,784 --> 00:30:24,447
<i>Sorry for the trouble.</i>

372
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:26,880
<i>Um, let me ask you something.</i>

373
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:29,107
<i>How did I get home?</i>

374
00:30:34,713 --> 00:30:37,413
<i>Fu Ming Yu got you back.</i>

375
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,135
I knew it.

376
00:30:42,480 --> 00:30:45,634
<i>What about Ruan Si Xian? Was she okay?</i>

377
00:30:48,494 --> 00:30:49,840
<i>She's fine.</i>

378
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:52,854
<i>She just slapped Fu Ming Yu in the face.</i>

379
00:30:58,284 --> 00:31:02,495
As expected of a female pilot.
She actually slapped him.

380
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:08,253
This is the world I've always wanted.

381
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:11,657
You An, I'm coming in.

382
00:31:13,362 --> 00:31:15,400
Look at you. Why did you drink so much?

383
00:31:15,400 --> 00:31:18,389
You must have a headache.
Here. I made you some honey water.

384
00:31:18,389 --> 00:31:20,208
Drink it.

385
00:31:20,208 --> 00:31:22,629
I have something to tell you.

386
00:31:22,629 --> 00:31:24,653
Do you remember
that female pilot from Hengshi Air?

387
00:31:24,653 --> 00:31:26,843
The one I took photos of.

388
00:31:28,627 --> 00:31:30,611
I vaguely remember her. What about her?

389
00:31:30,611 --> 00:31:32,524
Last night...

390
00:31:33,371 --> 00:31:36,000
she hit Fu Ming Yu.

391
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:38,773
- She hit Fu Ming Yu?
- And...

392
00:31:39,594 --> 00:31:41,378
it was a slap.

393
00:31:41,378 --> 00:31:42,523
Why?

394
00:31:42,523 --> 00:31:46,808
I was so drunk. How would I know why?

395
00:31:46,808 --> 00:31:51,617
But Fu Ming Yu had it coming. He deserved it.

396
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:57,363
Don't worry too much.
He's a grown man. One slap won't kill him.

397
00:31:57,960 --> 00:32:02,127
Last night, when he brought me back,
did you see his face? Was it swollen?

398
00:32:02,127 --> 00:32:05,671
He didn't bring you back. His chauffeur did.

399
00:32:05,671 --> 00:32:07,415
Then he deserved to be hit even more.

400
00:32:07,415 --> 00:32:10,499
I knew it. How could he possibly bring me back?

401
00:32:13,051 --> 00:32:16,841
I'm going to send Ruan
a congratulatory message.

402
00:32:25,520 --> 00:32:30,127
<i>My dear Ruan, you're really something.
That slap really satisfied my grudge.</i>

403
00:32:30,127 --> 00:32:33,035
<i>Sending this to congratulate you.
I'll treat you to a drink another day.</i>

404
00:32:34,158 --> 00:32:37,066
<i>More drinking? None of this would've happened
if you hadn't been drinking.</i>

405
00:32:37,066 --> 00:32:38,871
- If it hadn't happened--
- What do you mean?

406
00:32:38,871 --> 00:32:41,566
- Am I not welcome here?
- I wouldn't dare.

407
00:32:41,566 --> 00:32:43,105
I have a meeting with the Safety Committee.

408
00:32:43,105 --> 00:32:45,649
Mr. Fu takes it seriously.
So I came over myself.

409
00:32:45,649 --> 00:32:47,254
Captain Fan...

410
00:32:48,044 --> 00:32:49,920
Any chance of Captain Fan's return?

411
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:53,425
Who knows? It depends on today's simulation.
We'll see.

412
00:32:53,425 --> 00:32:55,991
- Alright, I'll leave you to it.
- Okay. Go ahead.

413
00:32:56,600 --> 00:33:00,901
That's why I'm telling you,
the data must be verified from now on.

414
00:33:00,901 --> 00:33:02,242
Let's go.

415
00:33:09,775 --> 00:33:12,250
What is this now?

416
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:16,347
Can't you tell? It's my workstation.

417
00:33:16,347 --> 00:33:17,941
A massage chair.

418
00:33:17,941 --> 00:33:20,605
Young master, did you come here to retire?

419
00:33:20,605 --> 00:33:22,960
Put yourself in my shoes.

420
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:26,675
How many days of hard labor have I done
for you? Can't I at least be comfortable?

421
00:33:26,675 --> 00:33:30,520
Should I prepare a fruit platter for you,
along with some tea?

422
00:33:30,520 --> 00:33:32,943
Maybe I should hire two people to wait on you.

423
00:33:32,943 --> 00:33:34,200
No need.

424
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:36,753
I have all of that back at Bo'ao Air.

425
00:33:37,600 --> 00:33:41,007
But seriously,
do you have any employee benefits here?

426
00:33:41,007 --> 00:33:43,660
For example, team-building activities?

427
00:33:44,320 --> 00:33:47,519
I've been under a lot of pressure lately.
I really need to go out and relax.

428
00:33:47,519 --> 00:33:50,651
I haven't even opened yet,
and you want team-building?

429
00:33:50,651 --> 00:33:53,228
Are you here to reform my workplace?

430
00:33:54,347 --> 00:33:56,851
I'm not joking.

431
00:33:56,851 --> 00:33:59,128
- I'll take you to Ma'ao.
- I'm not joking either.

432
00:33:59,128 --> 00:34:02,240
Look at the state of my studio,
and with things at my family...

433
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:04,520
How heartless would I have to be
to travel with you?

434
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,080
I'll cover all the expenses.

435
00:34:06,859 --> 00:34:09,204
Flights, hotels, and shopping.

436
00:34:09,204 --> 00:34:11,075
A one-stop service.

437
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:15,139
Well, I could consider it.

438
00:34:15,139 --> 00:34:18,235
But it has to be
after my parents' wedding anniversary.

439
00:34:18,235 --> 00:34:21,050
It's mainly for our team's cohesion.

440
00:34:21,050 --> 00:34:23,590
Boss, the massage chair is installed.
Please sign here.

441
00:34:25,219 --> 00:34:26,938
- Done.
- Thanks.

442
00:34:29,253 --> 00:34:32,476
Why do I feel like, with you in my studio,

443
00:34:32,476 --> 00:34:34,980
it'll go bankrupt sooner or later?

444
00:34:34,980 --> 00:34:39,829
Let me tell you, Zheng You An.
Your studio won't go bust because I'm here.

445
00:34:39,829 --> 00:34:44,078
Life is only 30,000 days.
Shouldn't I make myself comfortable?

446
00:34:46,066 --> 00:34:50,771
Today's simulated emergency
is based on Flight 2076 of Hengshi Air,

447
00:34:50,771 --> 00:34:53,434
where a passenger
suffered a sudden heart attack.

448
00:34:53,434 --> 00:34:57,760
Landing must be completed in 15 minutes
so the passenger can receive timely care.

449
00:34:57,760 --> 00:35:00,599
We have four simulators
with four different decisions.

450
00:35:00,599 --> 00:35:02,600
No.1 Simulator is Captain Fan.

451
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,394
She will maintain
the flight status of that day,

452
00:35:05,394 --> 00:35:07,167
keeping the bank angle under 45°.

453
00:35:07,167 --> 00:35:11,316
No.2 Simulator will avoid an overweight landing
by holding to consume fuel.

454
00:35:11,316 --> 00:35:14,425
No.3 Simulator will keep the autopilot engaged

455
00:35:14,425 --> 00:35:16,760
with a subsequent decision
for an overweight landing.

456
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:19,360
No.4 Simulator will also
disengage the autopilot,

457
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:21,760
matching Captain Fan's decision.

458
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:23,960
We can begin now.

459
00:35:25,827 --> 00:35:29,600
<i>- Jiang City, Hengshi Air 2076.
- Hengshi Air 2076, go ahead.</i>

460
00:35:29,600 --> 00:35:33,360
<i>A passenger has fainted on board.
A doctor is currently treating her.</i>

461
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:34,960
<i>But immediate emergency care is needed.</i>

462
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:36,840
<i>Request return to Jiang City and radar vectors.</i>

463
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:38,559
<i>Please notify our company
and relevant departments.</i>

464
00:35:38,559 --> 00:35:40,119
<i>Hengshi Air 2076, roger.</i>

465
00:35:40,119 --> 00:35:42,980
<i>Radar vectors. Turn right heading 210.
Descend to 4,200.</i>

466
00:35:44,189 --> 00:35:45,480
Descend to 4,200.

467
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:51,997
[No.1 Simulator: Autopilot disengaged]
[Bank angle less than 45°/ Status: Stable]

468
00:35:51,997 --> 00:35:53,760
[No.2 Simulator: Autopilot]
We are currently overweight.

469
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:56,560
Expect 30 minutes of holding to burn fuel.

470
00:35:56,560 --> 00:36:00,440
[No.3 Simulator: Autopilot]
We'll maintain autopilot. Bank angle under 30°.

471
00:36:00,440 --> 00:36:02,920
[No.4 Simulator: Autopilot disengaged]
No.4 Simulator. Disengage autopilot now.

472
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:05,644
[Status: Unstable]
Bank angle under 45°.

473
00:36:11,597 --> 00:36:15,090
Next, the four captains began landing.

474
00:36:15,987 --> 00:36:18,411
No.1 Simulator, prepare to land.

475
00:36:18,411 --> 00:36:19,471
<i>100.</i>

476
00:36:25,924 --> 00:36:27,080
<i>40.</i>

477
00:36:27,080 --> 00:36:28,135
<i>30.</i>

478
00:36:28,135 --> 00:36:29,154
<i>20.</i>

479
00:36:29,154 --> 00:36:30,261
<i>10.</i>

480
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:35,034
[No.1 Simulator: 9 min 45 sec]
[No warning triggered]

481
00:36:35,034 --> 00:36:37,674
<i>No.1 Simulator has landed.</i>

482
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:52,244
No.4 Simulator, prepare to land.

483
00:36:56,369 --> 00:36:59,200
[No.4 Simulator: 11 min 21 sec]
[Flight status: Unstable]

484
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:01,791
<i>No.4 Simulator has landed.</i>

485
00:37:17,197 --> 00:37:18,679
No.3 Simulator, prepare to land.

486
00:37:18,679 --> 00:37:19,600
<i>50.</i>

487
00:37:19,600 --> 00:37:20,784
<i>40.</i>

488
00:37:20,784 --> 00:37:21,794
<i>30.</i>

489
00:37:21,794 --> 00:37:22,800
<i>20.</i>

490
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:23,576
<i>10.</i>

491
00:37:23,576 --> 00:37:25,840
[No.3 Simulator: 15 min 15 sec]
[QAR 710 hard landing warning]

492
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:28,272
No.3 Simulator has landed.

493
00:37:28,272 --> 00:37:31,450
<i>No.2 Simulator.
Estimated landing in 15 minutes.</i>

494
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:55,306
No.2 Simulator has landed.

495
00:37:55,306 --> 00:37:58,682
[No.2 Simulator: 31 min 45 sec]
[No warning triggered]

496
00:38:04,268 --> 00:38:07,011
All four simulator crews have landed.

497
00:38:07,011 --> 00:38:11,555
As we can see,
No.2 Simulator chose to hold and burn fuel

498
00:38:11,555 --> 00:38:13,619
to avoid an overweight landing,

499
00:38:13,619 --> 00:38:16,720
extending its landing time
to 31 minutes and 45 seconds.

500
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:18,465
This took much longer than Captain Fan.

501
00:38:18,465 --> 00:38:20,969
It delayed the passenger's critical care.

502
00:38:20,969 --> 00:38:24,274
No.3 Simulator, during an overweight landing,

503
00:38:24,274 --> 00:38:26,720
it failed to control the plane's descent,

504
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,224
triggering a QAR hard landing warning.

505
00:38:29,224 --> 00:38:31,400
It took slightly over 15 minutes.

506
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:34,745
No.4 Simulator made the same decision
as Captain Fan.

507
00:38:34,745 --> 00:38:36,410
It disengaged autopilot

508
00:38:36,410 --> 00:38:40,393
and kept the bank angle
within the CAAC standard of 45 degrees.

509
00:38:40,393 --> 00:38:44,480
Although it landed successfully,
the aircraft was severely unstable.

510
00:38:44,480 --> 00:38:47,665
It also took 1 minute and 36 seconds longer
than Captain Fan's.

511
00:38:47,665 --> 00:38:50,928
As for Captain Fan's flight data
and performance,

512
00:38:50,928 --> 00:38:53,552
I'm sure you've all seen it for yourselves.

513
00:38:53,552 --> 00:38:55,473
I won't elaborate further.

514
00:38:57,720 --> 00:38:58,920
Here.

515
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:04,928
To save everyone's time,
I have another three sets of experimental data.

516
00:39:04,928 --> 00:39:09,673
All from simulation replays
of the same emergency.

517
00:39:09,673 --> 00:39:12,670
All the flight data is right here.

518
00:39:13,531 --> 00:39:17,395
The mission for these three simulations
was to avoid triggering the QAR.

519
00:39:17,395 --> 00:39:19,979
To avoid a hard landing, the three captains

520
00:39:19,979 --> 00:39:24,559
either chose to hold and burn fuel
or remained on autopilot.

521
00:39:24,559 --> 00:39:28,707
But they all exceeded
the 15-minute diversion requirement.

522
00:39:28,707 --> 00:39:32,651
They also missed
the patient's golden hour for rescue.

523
00:39:32,651 --> 00:39:36,988
Other results aside,
the only captain who landed within 15 minutes

524
00:39:36,988 --> 00:39:41,441
was still 1 minute and 36 seconds slower
than Captain Fan.

525
00:39:41,441 --> 00:39:43,211
1 minute and 36 seconds.

526
00:39:43,211 --> 00:39:45,650
It seems like a tiny margin,

527
00:39:45,650 --> 00:39:49,395
but it's highly likely to be the window
between life and death.

528
00:39:49,395 --> 00:39:53,600
Fortunately, this patient received
timely treatment that day

529
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:56,200
and is now recovering at home.

530
00:39:58,200 --> 00:40:03,120
[To SH2076 air crew: I'm eternally grateful
for saving my life. From Ms. Xu]

531
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:08,880
This banner is the passenger's recognition
and praise for our entire crew.

532
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:32,905
Our crew members used their expertise

533
00:40:32,905 --> 00:40:37,311
to save not only a life,
but also a family's future.

534
00:40:37,311 --> 00:40:40,735
They ensured the safety
of all the passengers on board

535
00:40:40,735 --> 00:40:43,711
and prevented a catastrophe.

536
00:40:46,042 --> 00:40:51,513
If we still ground a captain like this,
it will be a loss for all of Hengshi Air.

537
00:40:53,561 --> 00:40:56,425
At the same time, this emergency reminded us

538
00:40:56,425 --> 00:41:01,120
that the QAR shouldn't be
the only measure of flight performance.

539
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:04,834
Reforming the QAR is long overdue.

540
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:26,640
[Upon review, the Safety Committee
has decided to lift Fan Lei's grounding.]

541
00:41:28,896 --> 00:41:31,736
[Jiang City]

542
00:41:36,182 --> 00:41:37,719
Can I help you?

543
00:41:37,719 --> 00:41:41,356
Ruan, you seem like a nice person.

544
00:41:42,401 --> 00:41:44,991
You helped Captain Fan resume flying, right?

545
00:41:47,079 --> 00:41:49,800
- My mentor is back on flight duty?
- You didn't know?

546
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:52,618
I thought you asked Mr. Fu for help.

547
00:42:18,709 --> 00:42:20,011
Mom.

548
00:42:20,011 --> 00:42:21,859
You're back.

549
00:42:21,859 --> 00:42:24,098
Why are you standing there? Come here.

550
00:42:30,316 --> 00:42:33,061
You asked me to come back. What is it?

551
00:42:33,061 --> 00:42:35,844
Why are you wearing a mask this late at night?

552
00:42:35,844 --> 00:42:37,943
My face is having an allergic reaction.

553
00:42:40,106 --> 00:42:41,960
Here's the thing.

554
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:45,225
Mr. Zheng and his wife
are celebrating their wedding anniversary.

555
00:42:45,225 --> 00:42:46,409
They invited us.

556
00:42:46,409 --> 00:42:49,032
If it were anyone else, I'd just skip it.

557
00:42:49,032 --> 00:42:51,840
But they invited the whole family.

558
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:54,526
If only your dad and I go,
it wouldn't seem right.

559
00:42:55,304 --> 00:42:59,018
But can you go in your condition?

560
00:42:59,018 --> 00:43:00,203
I can. No problem.

561
00:43:00,203 --> 00:43:02,026
- Is it serious?
- Not at all.

562
00:43:02,026 --> 00:43:03,891
Take off the mask and let me see.

563
00:43:03,891 --> 00:43:05,600
- I'd better keep it on.
- Let me see.

564
00:43:05,600 --> 00:43:07,640
- Mom.
- Let me see.

565
00:43:07,640 --> 00:43:10,924
I'm fine. I've applied the medicine.
I don't want to pass it to you.

566
00:43:13,085 --> 00:43:16,098
By the way, I saw that pearl necklace of yours.

567
00:43:16,098 --> 00:43:17,923
It's been sitting there for several days now.

568
00:43:17,923 --> 00:43:19,960
Why haven't you given it away yet?

569
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:23,440
Perfect. You can give it to Zheng's wife.

570
00:43:24,467 --> 00:43:25,652
Okay.

571
00:43:25,652 --> 00:43:29,724
I wonder if Ms. Dong will like this ordinary.

572
00:43:30,520 --> 00:43:32,104
I just don't get it.

573
00:43:32,104 --> 00:43:36,210
It's a second marriage.
What's there to celebrate?

574
00:43:36,210 --> 00:43:39,513
To be honest, I don't even want you to go.

575
00:43:39,513 --> 00:43:41,298
It's bad luck.

576
00:43:41,298 --> 00:43:45,280
Mom. It's getting late.
You should get some rest. I'll head back now.

577
00:43:45,280 --> 00:43:47,502
- Head back where?
- Back to Mingchen.

578
00:43:48,907 --> 00:43:52,678
What's so good about Mingchen?
You don't even want to come home anymore.

